<!-- HEADER ENDS -->

These rules are subject to change over time by the officers.<br>
<br>
These rules are not up for debate. <br>
<br>
Each and every member of this guild is responsible to KNOW THE RULES.  Not reading is NOT a valid excuse.<br>
<br>
Not every raid will be a points raid.  Officers present will determine whether a raid is a "points raid" or not.  If a points raid is determined, the following rules apply.<br>
<br>
<strong><u>Points are determined by the following formula:</u></strong><br>
Points dropped / People present at raid = Points per person (rounded generously)<br>
<br>
They are <b>*NOT*</b> based on points spent.<br>
<br>
( example: 20 point item drops, 40 people are present = 1/2 point to each person )<br>
<br>
( example: 20 point item drops, 24 people present = 1 point to each person )<br>
<br>
( example: 10 point item drops, 40 people present = 1/2 point to each person )<br>
<br>
The rationale behind the generous rounding is that there will always be turnover in the guild with members coming and going.  If there are no extra points, we eventually wind up gaining less points than are spent.  Hopefully the rounding will keep things in balance.<br>
<br>
1.) Common point values:<br>
VS Legs = 10 points, <br>
Trak BP = 10 points, <br>
Thurg/PoG BP/Robe = 10 points, <br>
Thurg/PoG Melee/Priest legs = 10 points, <br>
All other Thurg/PoG quest drops = 1 point<BR>
ToV BP/Robe = 20 points, <br>
ToV Melee/Priest legs = 20 points <br>
ToV Caster legs = 4 points<BR>
ToV Melee/Priest/Caster arms = 4 points<BR>
ToV Melee/Priest/Caster gloves,bracer,boots,helm = 2 points<BR>
<br>
2.) Points on items will be determined by guild leaders/officers.<br>
<br>
3.) Items won on a guild raid may be turned back in to the coffer at the officers' discretion for their <B>current</B> point value (if any).<br>
<br>
4.) Key components such as VP sleepers etc. are to be looted by Guild Leaders first, then officers then raid members as decided by the leadership present.<br>
<br>
5.) Epic pieces will go to the person that is closest to completing their epic. If more then 1 person is at the same stage in their epic progress, then standard lotto will apply.<br>
<br>
6.) Only active 57+ Main characters allowed in for loot unless the item will rot. If no active mains 57+ want an item, an officer may decide who can roll.<br>
<br>
(Example of peoples alts that would loot: Jaxson/martan Vordion/auemir Tallas/lendys/stabzjoo. These are all cases where most have lvl 60 chars and almost always have 2 or more chars at a raid. This doesn’t mean every char can loot in a raid. Only 1 char can loot per raid.)<br>
<br>
6a.) Members joining the guild after 8/21/01 are *NOT* eligible for loot until they have earned 15 points.<br>
<br>
7.) You cannot go into debt on points (your points CANNOT go below 0) unless an officer deems the situation warrants it.<br>
<br>
8.) Different armor counts as different lottoes:<BR>
<BR>
<strong><u>INT CASTERS (nec/wiz/mag/enc):</u></strong> <br>
helm/arms/gloves/boots/bracer/legs - 1 lotto<br>
robe - separate lotto<br>
<br>
<strong><u>ALL OTHER CLASSES (dru/brd/rng/clr/shd/war/rog/pal/mnk/shm):</u></strong><br>
helm/arms/gloves/boots/bracer - 1 lotto<br>
bp/legs - separate lotto<br>
<br>
<u>SUMMARY (for rule 8):</u><br>
<br>
int casters: robe is one lotto, all other pieces are a separate lotto.<br>
<br>
all other classes: bp/legs is one lotto, all other pieces are a separate lotto.<br>
<br>
They are separate from each other and do not count toward or against one another.<br>
<br>
If someone wins something from 1 lotto, they are still eligible to win something from another lotto. <br>
<br>
If everyone in a given lotto has won a drop (Tenille won arms, Tallas won gloves, Xantar won helm) the lotto starts all over again - (Tallas, Tenille and Xantar may ALL roll again - assuming nobody else is rolling who has NOT won an item).<br>
<br>
9.) Rolls are conducted according to the tiers of the people rolling.  The points tiers are as follows:<BR>
<BR>
Tier 1: less than 20<BR>
Tier 2: 20-39.99<BR>
Tier 3: 40-59.99<BR>
Tier 4: 60-79.99<BR>
Tier 5: 80-99.99<BR>
Tier 6: 100-119.99<BR>
Tier 7: 120-139.99<BR>
Tier 8: 140-159.99<BR>
Tier 9: 160-179.99<BR>
Tier 10: 180-199.99<BR>
Tier 11: 200-219.99<BR>
etc..<BR>
<BR>
Your points tier is based on your current total points.  Points may be viewed by clicking <a href="point_report.cfm">here</a>.  The item in question is lottoed between all players wishing to win said item and having points at least equal to the value of the item in question.  The examples should clarify this:<BR>
<BR>
<strong><u>EXAMPLE 9.1</u></strong><BR>
ToV Quest Robe drops (20 point item)<BR>
<BR>
Greynor has 65 points (tier 4)<br>
Hansol has 150 points (tier 8)<br>
Majistikz has 136 points (tier 7)<br>
Sambus has 78 points (tier 4)<br>
<br>
Roll goes like this: Greynor 1 2 3 4, Hansol 5 6 7 8 9 10 11 12, Majistikz 13 14 15 16 17 18 19 20, Sambus 21 22 23 24<br>
<br>
2 is rolled, Greynor wins.<br>
<br>
Greynor has spent 20 points, leaving him on tier 3 with 45 points.<br>
<br>
<strong><u>EXAMPLE 9.2</u></strong><BR>
ToV Quest Arms drop (4 point item)<BR>
<BR>
Tallas has 95 points (tier 5)<br>
Tenille has 75 points (tier 4)<br>
Martan has 62 points (tier 4)<br>
Jenguran has 12 points (tier 1)<br>
<br>
All players want the item.  Tallas has won gloves earlier and Tenille has won boots earlier.  Gloves and boots are part of the same lotto as arms.  So Tenille and Tallas can't roll.  Martan and Jenguran are still eligible and they can both roll.<br>
<br>
Roll goes like this: Martan 1 2 3 4, Jenguran 5 <br>
<br>
Martan wins.<br>
<br>
Martan has spent 4 points, leaving him on tier 3 with 58 points.<br>
<br>
<strong><u>EXAMPLE 9.3</u></strong><BR>
Breastplate of Eradication drops (30 point item)<BR>
<BR>
Xantar has 95 points (tier 5)<br>
Shamooch has 103 points (tier 6)<br>
Tallas has 98 points (tier 5)<br>
Tuarreg has 110 points (tier 6)<br>
Bakk has 107 points (tier 6)<br>
<br>
All players may roll<br>
<br>
Roll goes like this: Xantar 1 2 3 4 5, Shamooch 6 7 8 9 10 11, Tallas 12 13 14 15 16, Tuarreg 17 18 19 20 21 22, Bakk 23 24 25 26 27 28<br>
<br>
1 is rolled, Xantar wins.<br>
<br>
Xantar has spent 30 points, leaving him on tier 4 with 65 points.<br>
<br>
<strong><u>EXAMPLE 9.4</u></strong><BR>
Twink item that everyone wants drops (0 point item)<BR>
<BR>
Tallas has 95 points (tier 7)<br>
Tenille has 75 points (tier 5)<br>
Martan has 62 points (tier 5)<br>
Jenguran has 12 points (tier 1)<br>
Xantar has 95 points (tier 7)<br>
Shamooch has 103 points (tier 7)<br>
Tallas has 98 points (tier 7)<br>
Tuarreg has 110 points (tier 8)<br>
Bakk has 107 points (tier 8)<br>
<br>
All players want the item, but it's a 0 point item and no points are spent here - so everyone can roll.  Everyone *ONLY* gets 1 roll.<br>
<br>
Roll goes like this: tallas 1, tenille 2, martan 3, jenguran 4, xantar 5, shamooch 6, tallas 7, tuarreg 8, bakk 9<br>
<br>
5 is rolled, Xantar wins.<br>
<br>
Xantar has spent 0 points.<br>
<br>
10.) The number of Points a player has are determined at the beginning of the raid.  When the raid starts, if you have 29 points, you may roll with 29 points and 29 points only.  This is to discourage players from using tradeable equipment won during a guild raid as points collateral during a lotto.  The only direction points will change during a raid is DOWNWARDS (as a player wins an item, points will be subtracted for the value of that item).  No points may be gained DURING a raid - they are only applied AFTER the raid concludes.<br>
<br>
11.) Points may also be given out at the officers' discretion for extenuating circumstances and heroic acts.  There is no way of documenting how this will take place, but we will make attempts to reward those who work hard.<br>
<br>
(example - The first time we killed Gorenaire - 5 bonus points were given to all present at the raid)<br>
<br>
11a.) Point value may sometimes be assigned in a situation where there is no loot for anyone.  ( example: Chardok King and Queen are now considered 5 point kills; all present gain their share of 5 points - 5 points divided by the number of people present.  After a few kills the points start adding up. )<br>
<br>
12.) A player is considered active only after he/she has attended 1 kill on at least 36% (rounded down) of the days during which we raided during the last 14 days.  For clarification - look at the points report, subtract 14 days from today's date, figure out how many of those days were "raid" days (this number will be at the top of your points detail page), take 35% of that, and round down.  Now figure out how many days during the last 14 days you have raided.  If it's less than the first number (the one posted at the top of your points detail page), you are not active.  Only active players are eligible for loot (see rule #6).<br>
<br>
For example: Today is 1/29/02 - go back 14 days to 1/15/02.  Between 1/15-1/29 - let's say we raided on 11 days.  36% of 11 is 3.96 - round down - you get 3.  So - you need to have raided on 3 days during this 14 day period.  Look at your points report and figure out how many days you raided on since 1/15 (you don't need to be there for the *entire* raid - just recorded for a kill during the raid.  Some raids have 5 kills, some have 1 kill.  If you were there for 1 kill, it counts as having been there).  If it's less than 3, you are not active.  If it's 3 or more, you are active.

